#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186161798 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "38398622-ca45-5eb6-a589-96aec162960a" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Joint Distribution of Two Discrete Random Variables"}] :question/id #uuid "2d698f44-e551-58a2-883b-3a992119bd76" :question/math-academy-id "e-9126" :question/problem "|  | $Y=0$ | $Y=1$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=0$ | $\\dfrac a2$ | $a$ |\n| $X=1$ | $a$ | $\\dfrac 52a$ |\n\nThe joint probability mass function $f(x,y)$ for the discrete random variables $X$ and $Y$ is given above. Find the value of $a.$" :question/worked-solution "The support of $X$ is $S_X = \\{0,1\\},$ the support of $Y$ is $S_Y = \\{0,1\\},$ and therefore the joint support $S$ is\n\n$$\nS= S_X\\times S_Y = \\left\\{(0,0),  (0,1),  (1,0),  (1,1) \\right\\}.\n$$\n\nSince we're given a joint probability distribution $f(x,y),$ we must have \n\n$$\n\\displaystyle \\sum\\limits_{(x,y) \\in S} f(x,y) = 1.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(0,0)+f(0,1)+f(1,0)+f(1,1) & =1 \\\\ \\frac{a}{2}+a+a+\\frac{5}{2}a & =1 \\\\ 5a & =1 \\\\ a & =\\frac{1}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186161808 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c0e20c64-85be-5cb5-acde-17ffd8b6aff5" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Joint Probability From a Table"}] :question/id #uuid "f2789f6c-11d5-5132-91b3-be65dac4ce24" :question/math-academy-id "e-9203" :question/problem "|  | $Y=1$ | $Y=3$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=2$ | $0.05$ | $0.25$ |\n| $X=4$ | $0.2$ | $0.05$ |\n| $X=6$ | $0.3$ | $0.15$ |\n\nCompute $P\\Big( (X,Y) \\in \\{(2,3), (6,1) \\}\\Big)$ given that the random variables $X$ and $Y$ have the joint probability mass function $f(x,y)$ shown in the table above." :question/worked-solution "Using the values in the table, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P((X,Y)\\in {(2,3),(6,1)}) & =P((X,Y)=(2,3))+P((X,Y)=(6,1)) \\\\  & =f(2,3)+f(6,1) \\\\  & =0.25+0.3 \\\\  & =0.55.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186161809 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "e247e2c9-3e47-5cf4-be8d-f1f22bb30b39" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Joint Probability Containing Inequalities From a Table"}] :question/id #uuid "01b86f31-f31e-567d-b798-fc0f10a4d0b1" :question/math-academy-id "e-9204" :question/problem "|  | $Y=0$ | $Y=2$ | $Y=4$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=0$ | $0.15$ | $0.1$ | $0.1$ |\n| $X=1$ | $0.05$ | $0.1$ | $0.05$ |\n| $X=2$ | $0.05$ | $0.25$ | $0.15$ |\n\nCompute $P\\left( X\\cdot Y \\geq 4 \\right)$ given that the random variables $X$ and $Y$ have the joint probability mass function $f(x,y)$ shown in the table above." :question/worked-solution "Using the values in the table, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X\\cdot Y\\ge 4) & =P((X,Y)\\in {(1,4),(2,2),(2,4)}) \\\\  & =P((X,Y)=(1,4))+P((X,Y)=(2,2))+P((X,Y)=(2,4)) \\\\  & =f(1,4)+f(2,2)+f(2,4) \\\\  & =0.05+0.25+0.15 \\\\  & =0.45.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162213 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c0e20c64-85be-5cb5-acde-17ffd8b6aff5" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Joint Probability From a Table"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8ec69fe3-66c6-5397-8465-9f723f7832c4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186158821} {:answer/id #uuid "e9c82e88-7188-53dc-9030-56290b21c77c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186158822} {:answer/id #uuid "06093776-36f6-5981-a2a9-c728d9cdc8db" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.25" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186158823} {:answer/id #uuid "2d5cfb2b-3e5a-5a29-a60a-dc96cdcfa570" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186158824} {:answer/id #uuid "744c410e-1aa1-531c-86db-96fe80839cfa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.35" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186158825}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8ec69fe3-66c6-5397-8465-9f723f7832c4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186158821} :answer-field/id #uuid "1c6215e2-457e-5495-a0c8-5aa564a0d446" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186158820}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "982b31fd-731a-56a2-a3eb-b1749eaecfdc" :question/math-academy-id "q-109335" :question/problem "|  | $Y=2$ | $Y=4$ | $Y=6$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=1$ | $0.1$ | $0.25$ | $0.25$ |\n| $X=2$ | $0.05$ | $0.15$ | $0.2$ |\n\nCompute $P((X,Y)\\in {(1,4),(1,6),(2,6)})$ given that the random variables $X$ and $Y$ have the joint probability mass function $f(x,y)$ shown in the table above." :question/worked-solution "Using the values in the table, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P((X,Y)\\in {(1,4),(1,6),(2,6)}) & =P((X,Y)=(1,4)) \\\\  & +P((X,Y)=(1,6)) \\\\  & +P((X,Y)=(2,6)) \\\\  & =f(1,4)+f(1,6)+f(2,6) \\\\  & =0.25+0.25+0.2 \\\\  & =0.7.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162224 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c0e20c64-85be-5cb5-acde-17ffd8b6aff5" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Joint Probability From a Table"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ccab9a42-516f-5dcc-9bfc-0927005b1fd1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186158887} {:answer/id #uuid "e4f3657a-03e3-508e-b19c-867e25d92c99" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186158888} {:answer/id #uuid "eff9ba0a-7bcf-5226-a8ab-343d19809e7a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{10}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186158889} {:answer/id #uuid "fa6f1304-27ea-53eb-9d9d-112cafba198b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186158890} {:answer/id #uuid "3211951a-cc10-5ead-9d86-39f1dc8a71da" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186158891}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ccab9a42-516f-5dcc-9bfc-0927005b1fd1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186158887} :answer-field/id #uuid "99d755f0-f3d7-5f63-8054-44b4c4d3c99d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186158886}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "3b94d2fe-04a5-5a10-9bc3-43bdb999a3a4" :question/math-academy-id "q-109686" :question/problem "|  | $Y=0$ | $Y=1$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=0$ | $\\frac{1}{4}$ | $\\frac{1}{2}$ |\n| $X=1$ | $\\frac{1}{8}$ | $\\frac{1}{8}$ |\n\nCalculate $P(X=0,Y=1)$ given that the random variables $X$ and $Y$ have the joint probability mass function $f(x,y)$ shown in the table above." :question/worked-solution "Using the table, we have\n\n$$\nP(X=0,Y=1)=f(0,1)=\\frac{1}{2}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186379117 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "38398622-ca45-5eb6-a589-96aec162960a" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Joint Distribution of Two Discrete Random Variables"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d558d5c8-497c-55aa-85ad-c12a4cf46985" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{10}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186379119} {:answer/id #uuid "25bc259b-5e05-5d7e-a8d7-8d17c6a02251" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186379120} {:answer/id #uuid "29b9faf8-a51e-5c0a-992d-7ed79b25828d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186379121} {:answer/id #uuid "d474ae32-4fdb-5a6f-b437-16424e4e19d9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186379122} {:answer/id #uuid "8f728fd2-c777-5b49-93a0-4684a42b9d5d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{7}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186379123}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d558d5c8-497c-55aa-85ad-c12a4cf46985" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{10}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186379119} :answer-field/id #uuid "f1730f85-24bc-5b7f-b3ff-a4fcef368824" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186379118}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "82fc220f-fc1d-5ac4-99ab-fda7a4300e19" :question/math-academy-id "q-110810" :question/problem "|  | $Y=1$ | $Y=2$ | $Y=3$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=0$ | $a$ | $2a$ | $a$ |\n| $X=1$ | $3a$ | $a$ | $2a$ |\n\nThe joint probability mass function $f(x,y)$ for the discrete random variables $X$ and $Y$ is given above. Find the value of $a.$" :question/worked-solution "The support of $X$ is ${S}_{X}={0,1},$ the support of $Y$ is ${S}_{Y}={1,2,3},$ and therefore the joint support $S$ is\n\n$$\nS={S}_{X}\\times {S}_{Y}={(0,1),(0,2),(0,3),(1,1),(1,2),(1,3)}.\n$$\n\nSince we're given a joint probability distribution $f(x,y),$ we must have \n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{(x,y)\\in S}f(x,y)=1.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(0,1)+f(0,2)+f(0,3)+f(1,1)+f(1,2)+f(1,3) & =1 \\\\ a+2a+a+3a+a+2a & =1 \\\\ 10a & =1 \\\\ a & =\\frac{1}{10}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186379124 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "38398622-ca45-5eb6-a589-96aec162960a" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Joint Distribution of Two Discrete Random Variables"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5f216c0c-b941-5832-a0e7-92a61fbba606" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{13}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186379126} {:answer/id #uuid "775b0a1c-49e7-54c1-98c9-55b3271efc2c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186379127} {:answer/id #uuid "713ee3ec-9773-5177-84a0-1e94c6397ff4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186379128} {:answer/id #uuid "b5f62b49-9fc8-5168-b7a0-00e426579938" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{17}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186379129} {:answer/id #uuid "f3a2896b-ef95-5889-a713-d3d2df3cb765" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{11}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186379130}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5f216c0c-b941-5832-a0e7-92a61fbba606" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{13}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186379126} :answer-field/id #uuid "c30a9dd6-3716-546c-81eb-535d6aad3030" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186379125}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "ded38983-0bd5-5a76-ae63-e605486f6707" :question/math-academy-id "q-110812" :question/problem "|  | $Y=0$ | $Y=1$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=1$ | $a$ | $2a$ |\n| $X=2$ | $\\frac{a}{2}$ | $5a$ |\n| $X=3$ | $3a$ | $\\frac{3a}{2}$ |\n\nThe joint probability mass function $f(x,y)$ for the discrete random variables $X$ and $Y$ is given above. Find the value of $a.$" :question/worked-solution "The support of $X$ is ${S}_{X}={1,2,3},$ the support of $Y$ is ${S}_{Y}={0,1},$ and therefore the joint support $S$ is\n\n$$\nS={S}_{X}\\times {S}_{Y}={(1,0),(1,1),(2,0),(2,1),(3,0),(3,1)}.\n$$\n\nSince we're given a joint probability distribution $f(x,y),$ we must have \n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{(x,y)\\in S}f(x,y)=1.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(1,0)+f(1,1)+f(2,0)+f(2,1)+f(3,0)+f(3,1) & =1 \\\\ a+2a+\\frac{a}{2}+5a+3a+\\frac{3a}{2} & =1 \\\\ 13a & =1 \\\\ a & =\\frac{1}{13}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186341707 :knowledge-poi